 - The team server (ADR 0026, a draft: part 5 of the journey; the sync client is part 6, ADR 0027; the runbook, part 7, is `docs/runbooks/team-server.md`, held to the code by `tests/unit/team-runbook.test.ts`): `wizardingcode-mem serve [--data <dir>] [--host] [--port] [--trust-proxy]` is a long-running process over its own SQLite `team.db` in `WIZARDINGCODE_MEM_TEAM_DATA` (default `<data dir>/team`), one process per directory by the lease `serve.lease`; it never opens a client's store and no hook imports `src/team/`. Every SQL statement lives in `src/team/store.ts` (`transaction` wraps `withWrite`; `db.ts` is the schema, the three opens and the statements an open runs before the store can be asked, the version read, the schema check, `secure_delete` and migration 1's identity write; `types.ts` is the leaf with `Limits`, `Context` and `Meta`; the `team-store-boundary` test fails on SQL anywhere else); the change signal, the leases, the rate buckets, the held-pull counts and the high-water file `feed.seq` assume that one process. Every request but `health` and `join` is authenticated by a device token (`wcm1_`, stored as a digest); invitations (`wci1_`) are admin-only; the alias filter of a pull is minimisation, not a permission (any member may read any item). Push applies items one by one in the spec's order (`push.ts`, `validate.ts`); pull reads the feed by a cursor and may `wait` up to 25 s (`feed.ts`); the mirror under `repos/` is an export written by `serve mirror` (`mirror.ts`, a child process the server runs hourly and a quiet minute after a push); erasure is the operator's `serve purge … --yes` (the replay it owes the repositories is noted in `meta` until whole, and the next run finishes it). Subcommands: `invite`, `invitations`, `invitation revoke`, `members`, `revoke`, `disable`, `enable`, `role`, `withdraw`, `reinstate`, `status`, `audit`, `mirror`, `purge`, `instance renew`, `health` (`src/cli/commands/serve.ts`; the log on standard error, their own output on standard output). Deployment: `Dockerfile` (a `pick` stage, user 10001, `/data`), `compose.yml` (hardened server behind Caddy), `Caddyfile`, `.env.example`; the release pushes the image to `ghcr.io/wizardingcode-io/wizardingcode-mem`. `src/core/redact.ts` names `team-token` and `team-invitation`. Tests: `tests/helpers/team.ts` (a server with an injected clock and timers), `tests/integration/team-*.test.ts`, `tests/unit/team-*.test.ts`, `tests/unit/deploy-files.test.ts`.
