-- The knowledge module (ADR 0024, a draft: part 1 the store, part 2 knowledge for the agent; no view yet): `src/modules/knowledge/`. The module (`index.ts`, share 0.2) reads the database and nothing else on a hook (`contribute.ts`): the pinned entries at every session start, once per context, within `SESSION_START_SHARE` (840 characters; D-9 (part 2), confirmed by the person on 2026-11-09), and on a prompt at most two entries that pass the lexical floor (`knowledgeEvidence` in `policy.ts`, `MIN_SHARED` 3), as information, not instructions; each shown entry is a `knowledge_shown` row. `visible.ts` (`visibleRepos`) is the one place that says which repositories a project sees. The probe `tests/fixtures/knowledge-probe.ts` (18 entries): 12 of 12 relevant prompts bring their entry first, 1 of 28 unrelated injects (the known "User roles" leak). The tools (`tools.ts`): `knowledge_search`, `knowledge_get` (both also with `--global`, over workspace and shared only) and `knowledge_propose`; a call opens the database, runs `openRepo` and `ensureFresh` under the lease (so it can write index rows; listing writes nothing); a propose runs the hourly rate (20 per agent id, `meta` `knowledge.rate:<id>`), the area, the target, the judge (`propose.ts`: `Judge.relate`, memory's `consolidate` logic and thresholds over at most 8 lexical neighbours, redacted, open proposals by the heuristic only; `makeJudge({ toolPath: true })`, `TOOL_JUDGE_TIMEOUT_MS` 3 s, no retries, usage under `typesafe.tools.*`, the breaker shared with distillation), then the store's write; a refusal is `refused <code>: …`. The agent id is the handshake's client name mapped by `agentIdFromClient` (`src/mcp/agent-id.ts`), `mcp --agent <id>` overrides, `mcp` otherwise, the OpenCode bridge `opencode`; a proposal is `proposed_by: agent:<id>` with `on_behalf_of` the person. The module's version is 8 (`0007_knowledge_agent.sql`: `pinned`, `fts_rowid`, the proposal's `contradicts`/`on_behalf_of`/`judged_by`/`judge_version`, `knowledge_fts` kept by the index writer, never by triggers, and `knowledge_shown`; `0008_knowledge_received.sql`: `knowledge_received`, the sync's copies of teammates' entries under the reserved repo id 0, with its indexes, ADR 0027). The drain runs `refreshStale` (at most `REFRESH_PER_DRAIN`, 3, repositories that differ from the disk; whatever the modules setting). `status` has a `knowledge` line; `doctor`'s knowledge check warns when the module is off, when the search table's rows differ from the active entries, and when the pins exceed the session-start share; `compact` removes the `knowledge_shown` rows of gone sessions and repositories. The store: the truth is Markdown files with frontmatter in one git repository per scope under the data directory (`<data dir>/knowledge/workspace`, `shared`, `projects/<folder>`; `entry.ts` is the formats, `repo.ts` the repositories and the one git runner `runGit`, `resolve.ts` the mapping of a project to its repository through its manifest, `store.ts` the writes, proposals and `adopt`, `taxonomy.ts` the areas, `index-store.ts` the index rebuilt from the files, `schema.ts` the leaf with `requireSchema`, which everything that reads or writes the tables calls). Every git call goes through `runGit`, never on a hook path, and never with the person's git configuration; `openRepo` is the one way to a repository, and before git runs it refuses a folder the store did not make (`refuseForeign`: one whose `.git` holds anything but regular files and folders included; `refuseLinkedRoots` for `knowledge/` and `knowledge/projects/` themselves) and a `.git/config` that holds anything but the settings `git init` writes (`checkRepoConfig`, an allow list: add to `ALLOWED_SETTINGS` only what the store itself writes); `statusOf` never looks into a nested repository. The store keeps no file of its own under `knowledge/` beside the repositories and the sync's `knowledge/received/` (ADR 0027, plain files `openRepo` never opens): git gets `/dev/null` as its global configuration, the repository's own `.git/config` (a file) as its hooks path, and no template. `doctor` is the one reader that does not go through `openRepo`, which writes: it reads by hand under the same guards (`refuseLinkedRoots`, `refuseForeign`, `checkRepoConfig`), each of which it must be given when `openRepo` gains one. Only a name with nothing at it is gone: the places that decide whether a repository is there, or which entry and proposal files it holds (the two roots, a repository's name, its `entries/` and `proposals/` folders and the names in them), ask the disk with `lookAt`, `kindAt` and `namesIn` (`repo.ts`), for which anything that cannot be looked at is a refusal, never "not there"; `doctor` lists the folders with the same three. The older `isDirectory` and `existsOnDisk` read any failure to look as "no" and are used only inside a repository, behind one of those refusals: never decide a repository's presence with them. A link or a file where a repository's folder was is refused by name and its index rows stay, and a project's row names its folder while anything is at that name (`matchProject` in `resolve.ts`), so no state of the disk gives a project a second folder. The index belongs to one data directory: `rebuild` refuses, forgetting nothing, where there is no `knowledge/` folder and the index holds repositories. An interrupted operation is put back by its intent record, path by path, only where a file is still as the engine left it; a record is read only when every path in it is the store's own (`ownPath`), and a path is followed only through real folders (`reachedByFolders`). Three rules live in one place each: the write of the engine's own text, with its record and its undo, in `commitChange` (`repo.ts`; `adopt` keeps its own frame in `store.ts`, since it gives a person's bytes back instead of restoring from HEAD); a step of `openRepo` under the repository's lease in `underOwnLease` (`repo.ts`); a command over several repositories, where one the store refuses is set aside, in `inEachRepo` (`index-store.ts`, with `isRefusal` in `errors.ts`). An agent's write is a proposal until a person accepts it; the entry point passes the writer, never the caller. A module's tables are versioned apart from the core schema in `module_migrations`: `src/store/migration.ts` is the `Migration` type, `src/engine/module-schemas.ts` the one list `openDb` reads (it imports migration lists, never module code), and `user_version` stays 7. Knowledge starts at module version 6 (1 to 5 were the withdrawn module's) and is at 8; a development store that ran 6 alone runs `knowledge rebuild` once. `wizardingcode-mem knowledge write | accept | reject | area | rebuild | adopt | list` is the store from a shell; `doctor` has a `knowledge` line. `wizardingcode-mem backup` does not copy the repositories. In tests, `tests/helpers/knowledge.ts` gives a data directory, a throwaway home and stores whose environment the test controls, and `tests/helpers/stub-git.ts` a git that fails or stalls on demand.
